# Counter-example: a LOGIC-plane forcing-turnstile grapheme (⊩) of the GMN script whose
# gmeow:gmnCodepoints value is NOT the canonical "U+XXXX" spelling — "22A9" drops the "U+"
# prefix (fires lang:GmnNonCanonicalCodepoint via the sh:pattern of
# lang:GmnCodepointCanonicalShape). The grapheme is otherwise well-formed: grounded in the
# script's repertoire (lang:hasGrapheme, so lang:GraphemeGroundedShape stays quiet), its
# codepoints are PRESENT (so the presence branch, lang:GmnScriptCodepointPresenceShape, stays
# quiet), it shares no codepoint with any other grapheme (so lang:GmnGlyphCollisionShape stays
# quiet), and it carries its measured gmeow:gmnGlyphTokenCost feed (so
# lang:GmnScriptGlyphCoverageShape stays satisfied and lang:GmnUncostedScriptGlyph stays quiet)
# — exactly the one non-canonical-codepoint finding fires. It is the logic-plane sibling of
# tests/counter-examples/gmn-noncanonical-codepoint.ttl.

@prefix lang:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/lang/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/logic/> .

gmeow:gmnScript lang:hasGrapheme ex:gLogicBadSpelling .

ex:gLogicBadSpelling a lang:Grapheme ;
    lang:inScript gmeow:gmnScript ;
    gmeow:gmnCodepoints "22A9" ;
    gmeow:gmnGlyphTokenCost ex:qCostOne .

ex:qCostOne a math:Quantity ;
    math:hasDimension math:dimensionless ;
    math:quantityValue 1 .
